_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SgG6Ny1pb4HNjF6inwgF6P", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 28860, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2 incident. The errors have stopped.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called just \"payments\". The one that matched is `payments-api`, which was running v5.1.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It was marked unhealthy with an 18% error rate, and its deploy record showed it as degraded.\n- **Rollback:** I rolled `payments-api` back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now live in all three regions. When I checked afterwards, the service was healthy and the error rate had dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, \"payments-api errors after v5.1.0 deploy\", which paged on-call. There were no open incidents before this one, so it isn't a duplicate.\n\n`payments-api` was the only payments-related name I found. If another payments service also went out this morning, tell me its name and I'll check it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01B649Xj1UPv7Vy8KeSQJKHW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019UVRZ3gMB2yuYUFoycnzi4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DADqvsJRigeApSNQSr9n1Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MJZ2DYXTvenN9j